; walk-s6x — the fine pattern delay lengthens the row it sits on.
;
; `S62` makes row 0 eight ticks instead of six, and `S00` on row 2
; recalls the whole `Sxy` its channel last saw. Channel 1's `S00` on row
; 3 remembers nothing, so it is no timing effect at all.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
